author ai
group features/gui
note Steps added from the Source, Symbols or References hang under the target: the step last selected in the tour being read. The reader needs it because without a target and a way back to top level, every added step would nest under whatever was selected last. The Source and Symbols views show it in a strip under their toolbars ('adds to startup under 1.2 fill') and the tour's steps list marks its row '+ adds here'. Press 'top level' in the strip and added steps go at the top level of the tour instead, until a step is selected again. Moving the selection off the tour (a symbol in Symbols, References or the graph) leaves the target where it was, which is what lets a reader collect several symbols under one step.

